' S-572 / S-360: `ABSTRACT CLASS` parses (the lexer used to read the word CLASS after ABSTRACT as an
' identifier, so the class was never declared) and a concrete subclass works through a base-typed variable.
ABSTRACT CLASS Shape
    PUBLIC
    VIRTUAL METHOD Area() AS I32
        RETURN 1
    END METHOD
END CLASS
CLASS Square EXTENDS Shape
    PUBLIC
    OVERRIDE METHOD Area() AS I32
        RETURN 4
    END METHOD
END CLASS
DIM s AS Shape = NEW Square()
PRINT s.Area()
